Subject: [PATCH] glassine: xwayland: a failed lazy (re)start closes the display instead of hanging X clients

Lazy Xwayland stopped spawning mid-session on the Glassine (image
21c75cf5): sway kept /tmp/.X11-unix/X0 and @X0 listening, no Xwayland
process, every X client hung in connect until the session restarted; the
log had nothing (sway hides INFO). handle_client_destroy ignores
server_start_lazy's result and xwayland_socket_connected ignores
server_start's: on failure the listening sockets stay open with nobody
watching them. Both now log at ERROR and close the display, so clients
are refused instead of hanging; the lazy cycle (exit, armed, start) is
logged too, to catch the trigger next time. Success path unchanged.

--- a/xwayland/server.c
+++ b/xwayland/server.c
@@ -211,8 +211,17 @@
 
 	if (time(NULL) - server->server_start > 5) {
 		if (server->options.lazy) {
-			wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "Restarting Xwayland (lazy)");
-			server_start_lazy(server);
+			/* glassine: logged at ERROR (sway hides INFO) so a lazy cycle can be
+			 * followed in sway.log; a failed re-arm left the X sockets
+			 * listening with no watcher: X clients hung in connect forever
+			 * . Close the display instead: they get refused */
+			wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "glassine: Xwayland exited, lazy restart armed on %s",
+				server->display_name);
+			if (!server_start_lazy(server)) {
+				wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "glassine: lazy Xwayland re-arm failed: closing %s",
+					server->display_name);
+				server_finish_display(server);
+			}
 		} else  {
 			wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "Restarting Xwayland");
 			server_start(server);
@@ -405,7 +414,12 @@
 	wl_event_source_remove(server->x_fd_read_event[1]);
 	server->x_fd_read_event[0] = server->x_fd_read_event[1] = NULL;
 
-	server_start(server);
+	wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "glassine: X client on %s: starting Xwayland (lazy)", server->display_name);
+	if (!server_start(server)) {
+		/* glassine: as in handle_client_destroy: nobody would watch the sockets */
+		wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "glassine: lazy Xwayland start failed: closing %s", server->display_name);
+		server_finish_display(server);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
